# =============================================================================
# summa filum — distributed sum-reduce admit inside @ nucleum
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Declared distributed sum — `reducta via summa ex … filum …` lowers to the
#     DistributedSum plan entry: cyclic per-lane term-body fold with exactly
#     one lane collective at group exit (Metal simd_sum, CUDA redux.sync,
#     WGSL shared-memory tree) and a broadcast result.
#   • Term body — per-lane scalar computation with exactly one valued
#     `redde`; local mutation of term-local bindings is allowed.
#   • Alignment — the source length must be a multiple of the 32-lane width
#     in v1; K = 32 here. Tails (K % 32 ≠ 0) decline at admission.
#   • Sequential spelling — omit `filum` for the portable host-lane fold
#     (see summa.fab for the identity-term oracle pair).
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • `filum` outside a `@ nucleum` kernel — declines (see summa-decline.fab)
#   • non-scalar terms — the term must be a numeric scalar
#     (fractus/numerus family)
#
# See also: summa, filum, nucleum, apud, tensor
# =============================================================================

@ nucleum
@ publica { }
functio column_dot(tensor<f32, [32]> a, varia tensor<f32, [1]> out) → vacuum {
    sit f32 total ← reducta via summa ex a apud [i] filum f sit s {
        varia f32 t ← s * 1.4140625
        redde t
    }
    out[0] ← total
}
